An SMS sent through telepathy-ring stayed "pending" in the event log for
ever: Conversations logs a sent message with the pending flag and keeps
its token as the event's "message-token" header, and the delivery report
(ring's, when the modem has sent the SMS) names that token; the report
then clears the flag. The token was taken from the sent message's header
(messageToken()), but telepathy-glib's message mixin passes it only as
MessageSent's argument, not in the header: the header stayed empty and
every report was "the original message for this delivery report was not
found". The sent token (Tp-Qt's sentMessageToken) when the header has
none. Leste's Conversations has the same code (found in the FreeBSD VM,
freebsd/modem/README.md).

--- a/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/tp/tp.cpp
@@ -787,7 +787,14 @@
   if (result.isNull()) {
     qWarning() << "Failed to add a database event";
   } else {
-    if (auto message_token = message.messageToken().toStdString(); !message_token.empty())
+    // the token the connection manager gave the message (MessageSent's
+    // token): telepathy-glib's message mixin does not put it in the sent
+    // message's header, so messageToken() is empty for ring's SMS, and the
+    // delivery report (whose original token it is) found no message
+    auto message_token = message.messageToken().toStdString();
+    if (message_token.empty())
+      message_token = sentMessageToken.toStdString();
+    if (!message_token.empty())
       rtcom_qt::set_event_header(result->event_id(), "message-token", message_token);
   }
 }
